        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "Changeable here (library code): crypto-browserify's shipped finite-field Diffie-Hellman API surface — index.js:47-51 re-export the `diffie-hellman` npm package (getDiffieHellman/createDiffieHellman/DiffieHellman*), so any browser bundle mapping Node's `crypto` to this polyfill gets classical finite-field DH with no post-quantum option. The 8 test sites are the project's own suite exercising RFC 3526 MODP groups modp1 (768-bit), modp2 (1024-bit), modp5 (1536-bit), modp14 (2048-bit), modp15/modp16"
